<section aria-labelledby="scdp-method-heading">
  <h2 id="scdp-method-heading">Spatial Conditioning with Visual Attention Anchors</h2>
  <p>
    A single global camera must capture both the workspace and the small visual details needed for precise manipulation. SCDP addresses this challenge
    by using intermediate end-effector trajectories as visual attention anchors. At each diffusion step, these trajectories identify locations in the
    image where the policy can gather task-relevant features.
  </p>
  <figure class="research-figure--wide">
    <a href="{{ '/assets/img/research/scdp/architecture.webp' | relative_url }}" aria-label="Open the full SCDP architecture diagram">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/img/research/scdp/architecture.webp' | relative_url }}"
        alt="SCDP architecture: multi-scale image features are sampled along reconstructed end-effector trajectories and condition successive action denoising steps."
        loading="lazy"
      >
    </a>
    <figcaption>A single RGB observation supplies global context and local features throughout action denoising.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Multi-scale image encoding.</strong> The visual encoder produces feature maps at several scales, retaining both broad scene context and
      fine visual detail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Spatial conditioning.</strong> Reconstructed end-effector trajectories are projected into the image. The model samples point-wise
      features from the multi-scale maps at these visual attention anchors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Conditional action denoising.</strong> The sampled spatial context conditions the action denoising network through FiLM and is updated
      at each denoising step.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>The implementation is available in the <a href="{{ project.code_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDP code repository</a>.</p>
</section>

